            <div xml:id="d980">

                <pb facs="0665" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg593"/>

                <head>Government of the Canton of St. Gall</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">St. Gall</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-03">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 3, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The chief justice and government council of the canton
                        of St. Gall to the Swiss Union council in Bern</hi>.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President and Gentlemen of the Council</hi>: As
                    we cannot refuse our approval of the Berne address of sympathy and condolence to
                    the government of the North American Union, we give it most cordially; and,
                    moreover, we are pleased to send an address to the government of the American
                    Union from our own government.</p>
                <p>In sending the original of it to you, we respectfully request you to have it
                    delivered into the hands of President Johnson.</p>
                <p>In the mean time we take the occasion to commend you as well as ourselves to the
                    protection of Divine Providence.</p>
                <p>In the name of the government council:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>SAILER, <hi rendition="#italic">Chief Justice</hi>.</item>
                            <item>ZINGG, <hi rendition="#italic">State Secretary</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
